# SENTINEL v2.9.0 — Credential Vault hygiene template (Phase 57)
#
# Copy these rules into your project's .gitignore BEFORE creating any vault
# or key file. The encryption key must NEVER live in code, Git, CI logs or
# any artifact that leaves the operator's machine.
#
#   cp .gitignore-vault >> .gitignore
#
# Access model: a key file (0600, 32 random bytes) is handed personally to
# an authorized party (tool designer / organization owner). Losing a key
# file means rotating it:  sentinel vault revoke --key-id <id>  re-randomizes
# the blob key so the removed key cannot open ANY copy of the vault file.

# vault files (encrypted at rest, but still not for Git)
*.vault
*.vault.json
sentinel-*.vault
vaults/

# authorized key files — the crown jewels
*.vaultkey
*.vault-key
*.key.json
sentinel-vault-key-*.json

# owner-reveal reports (contain PLAINTEXT credentials by definition)
credential-report-*.json
credential_exposure_report*.json
*-credential-report.json

# runtime scratch
.vault-tmp-*
results/*.vault
